  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "pageVersion": "sha256:e5167308dff34095064a4927606f2bb6321e8a99b63b275149462a7c07a4be37",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_caa768187ce144baaee0c2bfc4b9da5d",
      "statement": "The design distinguishes two kinds of ambiguity: lookup-resolvable (answer exists in the world, fixable via context or tools) and judgment-required (answer is the user's own preference/priority), and the layer's purpose is to keep these from being conflated.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://notes/03-instruction-resolution-gate.md#L18-L23",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8156c2adad0e168a60dc536c5e778afaead0c9d2a223c9bc5706b20afa3de943:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_91ebd97dddf44591959d8ad584cd8ef0",
      "statement": "Since the 2026-09-21 revision the pipeline is a loop: it loads the domain's slot schema, fills slots from context, searches lookup-type slots and asks with search results as options when unresolved, builds options for judgment-type slots, re-searches slots whose clues were just filled, and confirms the assembled prompt before execution, while a lookup-type slot can only be asked about after a search attempt.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://notes/03-instruction-resolution-gate.md#L25-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3a4359090925e77146f8d496b698c08c97cac2bacd338498c191b97d966df29e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9e248b0d5bef4c4ebdaf8c3d6a86e50a",
      "statement": "Revisiting the incident shows the actual failure was not a wrong comparison between looking up and asking, but that the comparison/deliberation step itself never ran and an empty slot value went straight to question generation reflexively.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://notes/03-instruction-resolution-gate.md#L75-L75",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1fff8c38b2fca0c130f874f314243c5c739e295a3a3addec956cf2e42ff8bab7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_40dfa5b87371476d995966713678e10b",
      "statement": "Because the skipped step was the deliberation itself, the design concludes the layer must be a structural gate enforced outside the model's reasoning process (e.g., a question-asking tool call is only permitted if a lookup-attempt record already exists for that slot) rather than a checklist the model is expected to follow.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://notes/03-instruction-resolution-gate.md#L79-L81",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4cd43f314d2fbceeae833768e61f1479929eb2c4533a535590643f6fa16e81b3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b2c77eb5a09544c6944c658b7f69aafc",
      "statement": "Applying the pipeline retrospectively to the incident: the GitHub account slot was classified as lookup-resolvable via existing conversation memory, and a gh api call against 28 starred repos narrowed to exactly one match (langchain-ai/openwiki), which would have let the pipeline proceed without asking the user.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://notes/03-instruction-resolution-gate.md#L92-L95",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d00535a0ce6fe6ac915712fe0c836963783741f48f07617d0522327cce7d6111:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d33abb693ab046c9887957c17ff26b8e",
      "statement": "The two original open questions (catching a lookup that resolves to a single wrong candidate, and classifying whether a slot is lookup-resolvable) now have design answers in the confirmation step and schema slot types, but neither has been implemented or tested.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://notes/03-instruction-resolution-gate.md#L103-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d89c3cb6771e3ba5c0711fcaba99fc44d403100e561b4ad0a49c0188424eb6f3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_25d5e4c8e2d1488abb9438a22cf35235",
      "statement": "Slots are predefined per domain, each tagged with a type (lookup or judgment), a lookup or option source, and dependencies, and the design treats knowing a domain's slot list as that domain's expertise.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://notes/03-instruction-resolution-gate.md#L49-L71",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:06e4b7a00dda05df80c1076fff4b44b5aca9cb2b61cceb7e123ef04cec55991d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_79e6779716fc41ae89b6fa64c6faf9b3",
      "statement": "After the loop the assembled prompt is shown once with each slot value's origin, to catch wrong unique lookups, and a question cap with visible defaults is proposed to limit question fatigue.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://notes/03-instruction-resolution-gate.md#L83-L88",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7b067456c185bec01ba7e239c1348f3bdf9a38b7cecfce2afea1b065a5ff31d9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dfba1915e92d42eca812638b479173c6",
      "statement": "notes/03's proposed question cap conflicts with the 2026-09-28 decision to keep asking until a clarity standard is met instead of capping questions.",
